            'authority_url' => 'https://hcigeorgetown.gov.in/pages/Njg2',
            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Amateur participation — a one-off tournament, a trial, a short training camp — reads, on the available evidence, as fitting within whichever general visitor/tourist entry route currently applies to Indian passport holders, subject to the unresolved visa-free-vs-visa-required conflict described above. No official source distinguishes "sport" from any other tourism purpose.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Professional, Paid or Contracted Engagement</h4><p>Nothing in the available sources confirms how Guyana treats a paid or contracted sporting engagement (for example, a professional cricketer or footballer signed to a Guyanese club or franchise). The Business Visa route, which the Indian High Commission in Georgetown documents, is built around a corporate/employer invitation rather than a sporting one, and no employment-visa or work-permit detail specific to athletes was found. This should be treated as not independently confirmed rather than assumed to be covered by either the tourist or business route.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Officials, Coaches and Support Staff</h4><p>No separate category for coaches, referees or technical staff was found; on the evidence available they would likely travel on the same visitor/tourist basis as competing amateurs, but this is not confirmed by an official source.</p>',
