            'eligibility_html' => '<p>A short, one-off competition trip (a tournament, a trial, a short training camp) appears to fall under Honduras\'s general tourist/visitor entry rather than any sports-specific category, subject to the unresolved visa-free-vs-visa-required conflict described above.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Professional/Contracted Athletes</h4><p>For a sustained, paid sporting engagement, Honduras is reported (via a third-party aggregator, not an official page reproduced directly) to offer a "Special Stay Permit — Athlete," consistent with the general "Special Stay Permit with Work Contract" that Honduras requires of any foreign national doing paid work. Reported requirements include a valid passport, recent photo, character/criminal-record check where applicable, proof of means of support, and registration as a foreign national after arrival. This is a residence/work-authorisation-type route, not a quick-turnaround competition visa, and should be treated as not fully confirmed given the thinness of the sourcing.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Coaches, Referees and Technical Staff</h4><p>No separate category for these roles was found; depending on whether their engagement is short and unpaid or sustained and paid, the same tourist-entry-versus-Special-Stay-Permit distinction described above would likely apply, but this is not independently confirmed.</p>',
