            'application_centre' => 'VFS Global (Switzerland visa application centre network) in India, or the Embassy of Switzerland, New Delhi',
            'authority_name' => 'Embassy of Switzerland (representing Liechtenstein) — Sport Events Schengen visa checklist',
            'authority_url' => 'https://www.eda.admin.ch/content/dam/countries/countries-content/kenia/en/Visa_Checklist_Sports.pdf',
            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Indian athletes, coaches, referees and team officials travelling to Liechtenstein to compete in or attend a sporting event apply for the ordinary Schengen short-stay (Type C) visa through the Embassy of Switzerland in New Delhi or VFS Global, and should use the "Sport Events" supporting-document checklist that Swiss missions publish for this purpose. Typical requirements seen on Swiss-mission sport-event checklists (for the broader Switzerland/Liechtenstein Schengen visa, since no Liechtenstein-specific checklist was located) include a signed, dated invitation letter from the event organiser naming the event and dates, confirmation of who funds the trip, Schengen-wide travel medical insurance of at least EUR 30,000, a round-trip flight booking, and accommodation confirmation.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Amateur vs Professional/Paid Participation</h4><p>A short-stay Schengen visa (including the sport-events category) does not authorise employment. Amateur participation and attending/competing in an event are consistent with the Type C visa; a paid or contracted professional engagement in Liechtenstein would be expected to require a work-authorised residence route instead, though this was not separately confirmed for Liechtenstein specifically in this research.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Competing Athletes, Coaches and Officials</h4><p>Apply for a Schengen short-stay (Type C) visa through the Embassy of Switzerland, New Delhi, or VFS Global, specifying Liechtenstein as the main destination and using the "Sport Events" supporting-document checklist. Have the event organiser send the invitation letter, arrange Schengen-wide medical insurance of at least EUR 30,000, and book your travel and accommodation before applying.</p><p>Our consultants can help confirm the current checklist and lead times with the Swiss mission before you submit your application.</p>',
