            'intro_html' => '<p>Macau is a Special Administrative Region of China with its own immigration and visa policy, independent of mainland China\'s rules (per a WebSearch snippet from the Wikipedia "Visa policy of Macau" summary, which states that Macau sets its immigration and visa policy independently from the rest of China). No sports-specific visa category for Macau was found. Multiple non-official sources consistently describe Indian ordinary-passport holders as able to enter Macau without a visa for short stays, most commonly cited as up to 30 days, though none of these is an official Macau government page, and the rules for stays beyond 30 days are inconsistent across sources (embassy application vs visa-on-arrival vs local extension).</p><p>A Portuguese consulate-general document found during this research ("Visto Nacional VR E5 — Atividade Desportiva Amadora") is a Portugal national-visa category issued by Portugal\'s consulate general in Macau/Hong Kong for travel to Portugal — it is not a Macau entry permit and should not be confused with one.</p>',
