            'eligibility_html' => '<p>No dedicated sports or athlete visa category for entry into Macau was located. Indian passport holders travelling to Macau to participate in or attend amateur sporting activity would, on the evidence found, use the same general visa-free short-stay entry (commonly cited as up to 30 days) available to Indian tourists generally. This was not confirmed against an official Macau SAR government page in this research, only against consistent third-party/commercial sources.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Amateur vs Paid/Professional Engagement</h4><p>Amateur participation or attendance appears consistent with the general visa-free visitor entry. A paid or contracted professional sporting engagement (for example, a contracted player or paid coach) would be expected to require Macau work authorisation rather than visitor entry, but the specific work-permit process for sportspersons was not independently confirmed in this research.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Not Mainland China</h4><p>Because Macau\'s immigration rules are set independently of mainland China, mainland Chinese visa categories (including any mainland sports-visa provisions) do not apply to Macau entry, and this record addresses Macau specifically.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Amateur Athletes and Short-Term Sports Visitors</h4><p>Most Indian sports travellers to Macau for amateur participation or short events can rely on the general visa-free entry commonly cited as up to 30 days, carrying a passport valid for at least six months, proof of onward travel and sufficient funds. Confirm the current rule with the Macau Immigration Department (Servico de Migracao) or the Chinese embassy/consulate in India before travel, since no official page could be directly verified here.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Professional/Contracted Engagements</h4><p>A formal paid contract (for example, with a Macau sports club) would likely need a Macau work-authorisation route rather than visitor entry. Our consultants can help confirm the correct category for your specific engagement.</p>',
